<% title "Organize a Ruby Event" %>

<% set_meta_tags description: "Start your own Ruby event. Whether it's a casual meetup at a bar or a full conference, the community needs more gatherings. Find guides, resources, and inspiration.",
     keywords: "organize ruby event, start ruby meetup, ruby conference organizer, ruby community, run a meetup",
     og: {title: "Organize a Ruby Event | RubyEvents.org", description: "Start your own Ruby event. Whether it's a casual meetup at a bar or a full conference, the community needs more gatherings. Find guides, resources, and inspiration."},
     twitter: {title: "Organize a Ruby Event | RubyEvents.org", description: "Start your own Ruby event. Whether it's a casual meetup at a bar or a full conference, the community needs more gatherings."} %>

<main>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="mb-4 text-4xl font-bold text-primary">Organize a Ruby Event</h1>

      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600">
        Every great community event started with someone deciding to bring people together. That someone could be you.
        The Ruby community is built by people who show up and people who create spaces for others to show up.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-12">
      <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold">It's Simpler Than You Think</h2>

        <div class="prose-lg text-gray-600">
          <p>
            When people hear "organize an event," they often picture months of planning, sponsors, venues, and
            logistics. But it doesn't have to be that way.
          </p>

          <p>
            Some of the most impactful Ruby gatherings are simple: a table at a restaurant, a few people with laptops at
            a coffee shop, or drinks at a bar after work. No slides required. No sponsors needed. Just Rubyists talking
            about Ruby.
          </p>

          <p>
            If there's no Ruby meetup in your city, <strong>you</strong> can be the one to start it. Post on social
            media, invite a few colleagues, pick a date and a place. That's it. Then
            <%= link_to "add it to RubyEvents", "https://github.com/rubyevents/rubyevents/blob/main/docs/ADDING_EVENTS.md", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer", class: "link link-primary" %>
            so other Rubyists in your area can find it. You'd be surprised how many people are waiting for someone to
            take the first step.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold">Event Format Ideas</h2>

        <p class="mb-6 text-gray-500">
          Not every event needs a stage and a projector. Here are some formats that work great.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-white p-6">
            <div class="mb-3 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10">
              <%= fa("utensils", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary") %>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Dinner Meetup</h3>

            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
              Reserve a table at a restaurant, pick a topic, and invite local Rubyists. Great food and great
              conversations, no setup required.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-white p-6">
            <div class="mb-3 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10">
              <%= fa("beer-mug-empty", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary") %>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Pub Night</h3>

            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
              The most casual format. Meet at a bar, chat about code (or not), and build friendships. Zero pressure,
              maximum fun.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-white p-6">
            <div class="mb-3 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10">
              <%= fa("laptop-code", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary") %>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Hack Night</h3>

            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
              Bring laptops, pick an open source project or a coding challenge, and hack together. Pair programming
              welcome. Coffee shop or co-working space works perfectly.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-white p-6">
            <div class="mb-3 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10">
              <%= fa("bolt", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary") %>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Lightning Talks</h3>

            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
              5-minute talks on any topic. Low pressure for speakers, high variety for attendees. A great way to
              encourage first-time speakers in your community.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-white p-6">
            <div class="mb-3 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10">
              <%= fa("book-open", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary") %>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Study Group</h3>

            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
              Pick a book, a gem, or a Ruby feature. Read a chapter each week and discuss it together. Works great for
              learning and building deeper connections.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-white p-6">
            <div class="mb-3 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10">
              <%= fa("building-columns", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary") %>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Conference</h3>

            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
              The big one. Multi-day, multiple tracks, sponsors, and a CFP. Start small. A single-day, single-track
              event is a great first step before scaling up.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-8 text-center">
        <div class="mx-auto mb-4 flex h-16 w-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10">
          <%= fa("book", size: :xl, class: "fill-primary") %>
        </div>

        <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold">The RubyEvents Organizer Guide</h2>

        <p class="mx-auto mb-4 max-w-xl text-gray-600">
          A comprehensive guide covering everything from finding a venue to managing speakers, handling sponsors, and
          building a community around your event.
        </p>

        <%= link_to "https://guides.rubyevents.org", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer", class: "btn btn-primary" do %>
          Read the guide <%= fa("arrow-up-right-from-square", class: "fill-current") %>
        <% end %>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-bold">Resources for Organizers</h2>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <%= link_to "https://evilmartians.com/chronicles/lets-have-more-tech-meetups-a-quick-start-guide-to-holding-your-own", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer", class: "flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl border border-base-300 bg-white hover:border-primary hover:shadow transition-all" do %>
            <%= fa("newspaper", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary shrink-0") %>

            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold">A quick-start guide to holding your own meetup</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Practical tips for starting a tech meetup by Evil Martians</div>
            </div>
          <% end %>

          <%= link_to "https://rubyconferenceproject.com/interviews/", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer", class: "flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl border border-base-300 bg-white hover:border-primary hover:shadow transition-all" do %>
            <%= fa("lightbulb", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary shrink-0") %>

            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold">Conference Organizing Insights</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Interviews and tips from Ruby conference organizers</div>
            </div>
          <% end %>

          <%= link_to events_path, class: "flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl border border-base-300 bg-white hover:border-primary hover:shadow transition-all" do %>
            <%= fa("calendar", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary shrink-0") %>

            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold">Browse existing events</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">See how other Ruby events are structured</div>
            </div>
          <% end %>

          <%= link_to continents_path, class: "flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl border border-base-300 bg-white hover:border-primary hover:shadow transition-all" do %>
            <%= fa("globe", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary shrink-0") %>

            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold">Events worldwide</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">See where Ruby events are happening, and where they're not yet</div>
            </div>
          <% end %>

          <%= link_to "https://join.slack.com/t/rubycentralcommunity/shared_invite/zt-41jguxsjq-imDu9pZ0zbNVe5ermzPskA", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer", class: "flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl border border-base-300 bg-white hover:border-primary hover:shadow transition-all" do %>
            <%= fa("comments", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary shrink-0") %>

            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold">#meetup-organizers on Slack</div>

              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">
                Join the Ruby Central Community Slack for advice, regular calls, and support from fellow organizers
              </div>
            </div>
          <% end %>

          <%= link_to "https://rubycentral.org", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer", class: "flex items-center gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl border border-base-300 bg-white hover:border-primary hover:shadow transition-all" do %>
            <%= fa("gem", size: :lg, class: "fill-primary shrink-0") %>

            <div>
              <div class="font-semibold">Ruby Central</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">The organization behind RubyConf and RailsConf</div>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </section>

      <%= render "page/community_cta", exclude: :organize %>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
